It is Tuesday morning.
The time is a quarter past eight.
I wheel my bicycle.
It is broken.
I go in to the bicycle mechanic.
He often works early.
The workshop is full of bicycles.
The bicycle mechanic looks up.
"Good morning," he says and smiles.
"Good morning," I say.
"My bicycle is broken."
He takes my bicycle.
"I am repairing it today," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I walk out of the workshop.
Now I walk the rest of the way.
I normally do not walk to work.
I always cycle.
But today I walk to the office.
It is a beautiful morning in February.
I am at work at a quarter to nine.
